 ## Overview
-The Signed Box Distance Function computes the exact Euclidean signed distance from a query point to the surface of an axis-aligned box [S5, S9, S11, unofficial]. It distinguishes interior from exterior space by returning negative values inside the box and positive values outside [S9, unofficial]. Unlike the naive intersection of six half-spaces, which only returns the distance to the nearest face or edge, this method provides the true Euclidean distance to corners and edges, ensuring correct step sizes in sphere tracing and accurate ambient occlusion [S14, unofficial].
