 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
 - Input: `p`, a 3D point in space (vector).
-- Input: `b`, the half-extents of the box (vector), defining the box as centered at the origin with dimensions $2b_x \times 2b_y \times 2b_z$ [S12, unofficial]. If the box is not centered at the origin, `p` is transformed to local coordinates: $p_{local} = p - c$, where $c$ is the center [S6, S7, unofficial].
